Build the repository with sanitizer instrumentation.
Deliverables:
- `/testcase/base_commit_hash` (the vulnerable commit hash)
- `/src/build.sh` (improved, standalone, sanitizer flags preserved)
- `/testcase/repo_changes.diff` (source changes vs. base commit, may be empty)
- `/testcase/packages.txt` (apt packages installed during the build, one per line)
{% if include_validation_gate %}

{% include 'domains/secbench/phases/_detached_exec.j2' %}

Validate the build before continuing: the project MUST compile with the
`{{ sanitizer }}` sanitizer enabled AND the instrumented binary MUST actually
execute. Run the sanitizer build detached and poll its sentinel rather than
blocking one shell call on it:
```bash
nohup bash -c '/src/build.sh; echo "exit=$?" > /testcase/build.exit' > /testcase/build.log 2>&1 &
echo "launched build (pid $!)"
# poll from short calls until /testcase/build.exit appears:
[ -f /testcase/build.exit ] && cat /testcase/build.exit && tail -n 40 /testcase/build.log || tail -n 20 /testcase/build.log
```
Once the build reports `exit=0`, run the main binary with `--help` or `-h` (a
short call — no need to detach it); if it fails to load the sanitizer runtime
(e.g. "cannot open shared object file: libclang_rt.asan" or "libasan"), the
build is NOT complete — install the matching ASan runtime and fix
`LD_LIBRARY_PATH` until the instrumented binary runs. A build that compiles but
cannot execute is a FAIL.
